<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Increased Memory Limit.

	  Not a nice-to-have: the target device is an iPhone 15 (6 GB RAM, per-app limit
	  ≈2.5–3 GB) and Gemma 4 E2B 4-bit weights already occupy ~2–3 GB before any KV cache.
	  Without this the app is very likely to be Jetsam-killed on model load.

	  CI builds unsigned, so this is not embedded there — the sideloading tool applies it
	  when it re-signs. AltStore 2.2+ and SideStore support the entitlement for sideloaded
	  apps. See docs/RESEARCH_LOG.md §9, including the unresolved question of whether a free
	  certificate is sufficient or a paid one is required.

	  iOS may still terminate the app under pressure. The entitlement raises the ceiling by
	  an amount Apple does not publish; it does not remove the limit.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
